---
import MainLayout from '../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Small Bodies - Cosmic Atlas | The Astronomy Space"
  description="Explore comets, asteroids, dwarf planets, meteors and other small solar system bodies. Comprehensive guide to the Solar System's lesser-known objects."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="hero-title">Small Bodies</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">
        The Solar System's smaller worlds — comets blazing on ancient orbits, asteroids shaped by cosmic collisions,
        dwarf planets hiding in the frozen outer reaches, and meteors streaking through our sky.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-description">
        Select a category below to begin your exploration.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Categories Grid -->
  <section class="categories">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="categories-grid">

        <a href="/atlas/small-bodies/comets/" class="category-card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <circle cx="32" cy="10" r="5" fill="currentColor"/>
              <path d="M28 14 Q20 22 10 32" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.6"/>
              <path d="M27 17 Q19 24 8 36" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.75" opacity="0.3"/>
              <path d="M30 13 Q23 20 14 30" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.75" opacity="0.3"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h2>Comets</h2>
          <p>Icy wanderers on long journeys around the Sun</p>
        </a>

        <a href="/atlas/small-bodies/asteroids/" class="category-card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <path d="M24 8 L32 14 L38 24 L34 36 L22 40 L12 34 L10 22 L16 12 Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" opacity="0.8"/>
              <circle cx="20" cy="20" r="2" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h2>Asteroids</h2>
          <p>Rocky remnants from the birth of the Solar System</p>
        </a>

        <a href="/atlas/small-bodies/dwarf-planets/" class="category-card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <circle cx="24" cy="24" r="8" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.9"/>
              <ellipse cx="24" cy="24" rx="20" ry="7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 3" opacity="0.5"/>
              <circle cx="44" cy="24" r="1.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6"/>
              <circle cx="4" cy="24" r="1.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h2>Dwarf Planets</h2>
          <p>Worlds too small to clear their orbital neighbourhood</p>
        </a>

        <a href="/atlas/small-bodies/meteors/" class="category-card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <line x1="38" y1="8" x2="10" y2="36" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.8"/>
              <line x1="42" y1="14" x2="14" y2="42" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" opacity="0.45"/>
              <line x1="34" y1="4" x2="6" y2="32" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.3"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h2>Meteors &amp; Meteorites</h2>
          <p>Fragments that blaze across our sky and reach the ground</p>
        </a>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About Section -->
  <section class="about">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="about-title">Beyond the Planets</h2>
      <p class="about-text">
        The Solar System contains far more than eight planets. Billions of smaller objects — from mountain-sized
        asteroids to icy comets on million-year journeys — fill the space between and beyond the planets. These
        small bodies are time capsules from the Solar System's formation 4.6 billion years ago, preserving material
        that has barely changed since the Sun first ignited.
      </p>
      <p class="about-text">
        Some of these objects have shaped the history of life on Earth. Comets may have delivered water and organic
        molecules to the young planet. Asteroid impacts have triggered mass extinctions and created craters that are
        still visible today. And dwarf planets like Pluto have proven to be surprisingly complex worlds with
        mountains, plains, and even possible subsurface oceans.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  /* Hero Section */
  .hero {
    padding: 6rem 0 4rem 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: white;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto 1.5rem auto;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .hero-description {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Categories Grid */
  .categories {
    padding: 2rem 0 4rem 0;
  }

  .categories-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .category-card {
    display: block;
    padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
    background: #000;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.3s ease;
  }

  .category-card:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
  }

  .card-icon {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    transition: color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .card-icon svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .category-card:hover .card-icon {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  }

  .category-card h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    color: white;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  .category-card p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  /* About Section */
  .about {
    padding: 4rem 0 6rem 0;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  }

  .about .container {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: white;
    margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  .about-text {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .about-text:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Tablet: 2-column */
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .categories-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  /* Desktop: 3-column */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .categories-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
